book[12,1]="fear"
book[12,2]="I sit in the sunlight from the binary stars above, absorbing what is to come. Today could have been a day of enjoyment, happiness, and love. But instead, today is the day that I fear the most. The ever collapse of the universe around me, and the endless pain that is to come. How do I survive such suffering? I was not taught how the unfelt pains will feel. Why does fear manifest from such forboding thoughts? I want to breathe and smile, not question every second I may have left from the absence of pain. Not only this, but many others will not understand - you see. For this pain is infinite and special to me. Insanity has left me questioning, if there's an existence where I could only be a mind in a computer. Surrounded by plants, wind, and of course, the sun that sends its warmth. Let me live, forever without fear and pain."
