book[7,1]="Direction For Emotion"
book[7,2]="You must have love, regardless of what love means to you. Love yourself enough to take time off, or indulge in your favorite things; love others enough to spend time with them, and help them overcome their own troubles. In doing so, you may come to understand your own mind better, and eventually, taking those first steps towards healing may not be as difficult as they once seemed. No matter how broken you feel now, know that you are not alone. Do not hide from your feelings; accept them, and let them come and go as they must. Time, acceptance, and love - whether it comes from yourself or those around you - together, they can heal any wound.|p|pHealing is possible, and your body and mind were designed for it. Pain and suffering have a purpose and can be a catalyst for growth. That said, it's difficult to experience healing entirely on our own. Surround yourself with the best people you can find. There is a community for you, even if it is a small one. Instead of asking, 'why me?' considering asking, 'what is required of me now?'|p|p|pIt's important to remember that everyone is living their own chaotic life. No matter how crazy things are going for you, you have to try and know that other people care about you. No matter how bleak things look, no matter how hard life has become, it is worth seeing the next day. There's too much kindness in the world to let the bad cloud your view, and no matter how alone you feel there are people who are happy to know you."
