book[2,2]=" |p|pThey said a virus was coming towards us. Out of nowhere, it spawned, consuming things. There wasn't enough time to study it, or act slowly. We ran as fast as our feet and vehicles could take us, which unfortunately wasn't fast enough.|p I managed to escape to the Science Facility which connects to The Origin. But even through the many doors, the virus will eventually find me. I don't know what it is, at all. The only moment I had to look at it, it didn't even make sense. The shape was almost four-dimensional in the way it moved, I'm not sure. I couldn't even see the form of it, only the red outer radiance that surrounded the horrible manifestations.|nIs it even a virus? I have no idea. I don't know any more. All my friends and family fled the planet before I got the chance to flee myself. Would I feel like a coward fleeing? I am not sure of that either. But all I know is that I have enough food and water for maybe a few days.|p|p|p|p|p|nI hear a horrendous cracking and buzzing coming from outside the door.|nIt's here."
